       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg add little blood pressure benefit and raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia.\n\nCould you check whether 20 mg is what you meant? Here are some options:\n\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, a typical starting dose. You can titrate to 10 mg after 1\u20132 weeks.\n- **Another agent added to amlodipine**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic. This is usually preferred if 10 mg isn't enough.\n\nIf you do want 20 mg for a specific reason, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting the rationale. I'll enter whichever dose you confirm."
